      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.1 State Legislature"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Telangana's State Legislature consists of the Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha) headed by the Speaker.",
        "The State Executive is constitutionally headed by the Governor and administratively led by the Chief Minister.",
        "The Judiciary is headed by the High Court of Telangana, overseeing law enforcement and administration of justice.",
        "Grassroots democratic governance is divided into Panchayati Raj institutions for rural areas and Urban Local Bodies (ULBs) for towns and cities.",
        "Official State Symbols embody the distinct cultural, natural, and historical identity of Telangana."
      ],
      "id": "zyclhub"
    },
